WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Hera has resolved Didymos and Dymorphos as separate asteroids 197 million kilometers away. This is Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 236. Four volunteers leaving a Mars analog, early designs for a flagship observatory, and cosmic spotlight. The European Space Agency's Hera spacecraft captured its first resolved images of the Didymos Dymorphos pair on October 18th, at a distance of 1,280 kilometers. Dymorphos appears as roughly one

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.700
pixel clearly separated from the larger parent body. The image followed two

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.120
breaking maneuvers that slowed the spacecraft to 20 meters per second

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:43.120
relative to the asteroids. Didi most measures 780 meters across, while

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:49.200
dimorphos spans 151 meters, orbiting an average 1.15 kilometers apart.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.220
Mission manager Ian Carnelli noted the team will obtain the first detailed images

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:58.440
of dimorphos on November 25th, examining the 2022

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.340
dark impact that sent debris across 10,000 kilometers of space, and shortened

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:08.720
dimorphosis orbital period by 33 minutes. Hara will later deploy two cube

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:13.160
sats for closer surveys before attempting a landing on the smaller body, and

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:17.220
those November observations will examine whether the impact left a crater or

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.136
reshape the asteroid entirely. Four volunteers will exit the crew health and

00:01:22.136 --> 00:01:27.416
performance exploration analog habitat at Johnson Space Center on October 31st

00:01:27.416 --> 00:01:34.176
after 378 days of isolation. NASA reports. The crew conducted simulated space walks,

00:01:34.516 --> 00:01:39.676
grew plants, performed habitat maintenance, and operated under communication delays and resource

00:01:39.676 --> 00:01:45.516
limits. Data collected will inform food system design, crew time efficiency, and behavioral

00:01:45.516 --> 00:01:51.296
support for future Artemis and deep space missions. Johnson Center Director Vanessa Whitech and

00:01:51.296 --> 00:01:57.176
NASA astronaut Jack Hathaway will provide remarks during the exit ceremony with live coverage

00:01:57.176 --> 00:01:59.036
on NASA Johnson's YouTube channel.

00:01:59.716 --> 00:02:04.556
The four crew members, Ross Elder, Ellen Ellis, James Spicer, and Matthew Montgomery,

00:02:05.056 --> 00:02:06.636
will also speak after emerging.

00:02:07.376 --> 00:02:13.696
The 1,700-square-foot 3D-printed facility simulated stressors expected on long-duration lunar

00:02:13.696 --> 00:02:18.436
and Mars flights, and health and performance measurements from the mission will help optimize

00:02:18.436 --> 00:02:21.036
medical care and psychological support practices.

00:02:21.036 --> 00:02:27.906
A June 2026 study in the Journal of Astronomical Telescopes, Instruments, and Systems, covered

00:02:27.906 --> 00:02:32.786
by Universe Today, outlines three exploratory analytic cases for the habitable worlds

00:02:32.786 --> 00:02:33.606
observatory.

00:02:34.086 --> 00:02:39.846
EAC-1 uses a 6 meter inscribed 7.2 meter circumscribed off-axis mirror.

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:47.546
EAC-2 adopts a 6 meter round off-axis design, and EAC-3 specifies an 8 meter outer diameter

00:02:47.546 --> 00:02:48.606
on-axis mirror.

00:02:48.606 --> 00:02:54.126
The system's engineering team favored off-axis architectures for unobstructed light collection

00:02:54.126 --> 00:02:59.866
and larger apertures to improve coronagraph performance, and to end modeling has been completed

00:02:59.866 --> 00:03:02.606
for EAC-1 and shared with industry partners.

00:03:03.166 --> 00:03:08.386
The coronagraph instrument blocks starlight to enable direct imaging of Earth-like exoplanets,

00:03:08.686 --> 00:03:12.546
and temperature control properties were also examined because they strongly affect

00:03:12.546 --> 00:03:13.986
light collecting efficiency.

00:03:13.986 --> 00:03:19.786
The habitable world's observatory remains scheduled for launch in the 2040s and is intended

00:03:19.786 --> 00:03:24.146
to succeed the James Webb Space Telescope as NASA's flagship observatory.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:29.964
Researchers from Kyushu University and the Max Planck Institute for Extraterrestrial Physics

00:03:30.474 --> 00:03:37.184
observed the L-154 pre-stellar core in the Taurus molecular complex 140-PAR-SEX away.

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:43.244
They measured a velocity difference between the ion tracer N2D-plus and the neutral tracer

00:03:43.244 --> 00:03:47.244
para-NH2D using the IRAM 30-meter telescope.

00:03:47.884 --> 00:03:52.484
Neutral particles are decoupling from magnetic field lines in a process called ambipolar

00:03:52.484 --> 00:03:55.324
diffusion, falling inward faster than ions.

00:03:56.124 --> 00:04:01.144
Prestellar cores in the study region reach temperatures between 10 and 30 Kelvin, cold

00:04:01.144 --> 00:04:03.904
enough for complex molecules to form on dust grains.

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:09.744
Lead researcher Doris Arzumanian explained that strong magnetic fields can otherwise delay

00:04:09.744 --> 00:04:10.224
collapse.

00:04:10.224 --> 00:04:17.184
The velocity offset provides the first direct measurement of ion neutral drift on the scales where stars actually form.

00:04:18.119 --> 00:04:23.559
A pre-stellar core, the size of a modest city block, can contain several solar masses of gas and dust,

00:04:24.079 --> 00:04:29.439
yet magnetic fields threading the larger cloud often act like rigid scaffolding that prevents collapse.

00:04:30.119 --> 00:04:38.919
In that tourist core, the ion tracer stayed tightly coupled to the field lines, while the neutral gas slipped ahead at 0.05 km per second.

00:04:38.919 --> 00:04:42.339
That small offset is the moment gravity starts to win.

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:47.079
The process begins once the core grows dense enough to block external starlight.

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:53.019
With fewer ionizing photons reaching the interior, the fraction of charged particles drop sharply.

00:04:53.639 --> 00:04:56.579
Neutral molecules no longer feel the magnetic field directly.

00:04:57.079 --> 00:05:01.059
They only collide occasionally with the sparse ions that remain tied to the lines.

00:05:01.759 --> 00:05:06.759
Over thousands of years, those gentle collisions transfer momentum, but the neutral still pull

00:05:06.759 --> 00:05:12.099
ahead. As they accumulate at the center they bend the field lines outward, reducing the magnetic

00:05:12.099 --> 00:05:17.199
pressure that once supported the core against gravity. Even while that supports slower roads,

00:05:17.759 --> 00:05:22.139
the interior stays cold enough for complex chemistry to proceed on dust grain surfaces.

00:05:22.819 --> 00:05:26.959
The same spectra that recorded the drift also show the core is chemically rich,

00:05:27.379 --> 00:05:32.879
with molecules that could serve as precursors to prebiotic compounds. What remains unknown is

00:05:32.879 --> 00:05:37.739
whether every pre-stellar core experiences this decoupling, or whether some collapse through

00:05:37.739 --> 00:05:39.839
turbulence or external compression alone.

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:45.219
Future high-resolution maps of additional cores will reveal whether that velocity signature

00:05:45.219 --> 00:05:50.059
is universal, or whether stronger initial fields can suppress the process entirely.

00:05:51.026 --> 00:05:56.026
Curiosity has driven a few meters past the chew-chew block to target the newly-named Nazca

00:05:56.026 --> 00:05:59.026
site for its next drill campaign, according to NASA.

00:05:59.026 --> 00:06:04.346
Post-drive imaging revealed abundant disc and needle-shaped crystal forms at the location.

00:06:04.866 --> 00:06:10.626
The rover will perform a quantitative relief model observation with Mally and a 150 shot

00:06:10.626 --> 00:06:14.586
depth profile LEBS measurement on a nearby target called Toucan.

00:06:15.466 --> 00:06:21.506
Additional LEBS, DRT, and APXS observations will characterize the surface before the preload

00:06:21.506 --> 00:06:21.966
test.

00:06:22.566 --> 00:06:26.966
The crystal forms may represent pseudomorphs whose original mineral composition has been

00:06:26.966 --> 00:06:32.726
replaced, and a finely layered texture on a nearby block named Condor will also receive

00:06:32.726 --> 00:06:33.726
L.E.B.S. analysis.

00:06:34.466 --> 00:06:39.106
The campaign follows the earlier Basque Lakes drill and aims to understand how the distinctive

00:06:39.106 --> 00:06:41.686
shapes formed under ancient Martian conditions.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:48.908
Ganymede passed in front of Io as seen from Earth on October 20th, 2026, producing a mutual

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:51.688
occultation recorded by astronomer Michael Wong.

00:06:51.688 --> 00:06:56.748
long. The event occurs when Jupiter reaches equinox and its Galilean moons appear ed

00:06:56.748 --> 00:07:00.708
John from our viewpoint. A geometry that repeats every six years.

00:07:01.328 --> 00:07:06.448
Ganymede's shadow also falls across Jupiter's cloud tops, creating a solar eclipse for any

00:07:06.448 --> 00:07:12.448
hypothetical observers on the planet. Jupiter currently has 115 known moons, second

00:07:12.448 --> 00:07:19.348
only to Saturn. The video shows the precise moment Ganymede blocks IO from view. Mutual occultations

00:07:19.348 --> 00:07:24.368
of the Galilean moons remain rare because they require Earth's precise alignment with the orbital

00:07:24.368 --> 00:07:30.672
plane. A scientist examining early data from the Simone survey telescope identified the distant

00:07:30.672 --> 00:07:39.452
icy body 2026 ED 138 beyond Pluto's orbit. Fizz.org reports. The object is provisionally classified

00:07:39.452 --> 00:07:45.112
as a dwarf planet candidate and represents the first such discovery credited to the NSF DOE

00:07:45.112 --> 00:07:50.632
vericirubin observatory. The body orbits in the outer solar system and was spotted during

00:07:50.632 --> 00:07:56.552
routine processing of survey images. Its detection demonstrates the telescope's capability to identify

00:07:56.552 --> 00:08:03.512
faint, slow-moving objects at great distances. Observations with ESO's very large telescope reveal

00:08:03.512 --> 00:08:09.032
a rare double debris disk around a white dwarf, with the two components separated by a clear gap.

00:08:09.712 --> 00:08:14.032
Planetary bodies, one possibly Pluto-sized, appear to be shaping the structure.

00:08:14.032 --> 00:08:19.052
The disc consists of material from planets destroyed during the star's red giant phase.

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:24.572
The gap suggests ongoing dynamical clearing by surviving planets that avoided engulfment.

00:08:25.092 --> 00:08:29.432
This configuration offers a glimpse of what may happen to our own solar system once the

00:08:29.432 --> 00:08:30.672
sun becomes a white dwarf.

00:08:32.076 --> 00:08:38.116
Contracts signed on October 23rd and 26th expand the Galileo 2nd generation fleet to 16 satellites.

00:08:38.676 --> 00:08:40.536
The European Space Agency announced.

00:08:40.536 --> 00:08:45.616
Thales, Elania, Space, and Airbus defense in space will each build two more spacecraft

00:08:45.616 --> 00:08:48.096
identical to the six already under contract.

00:08:48.716 --> 00:08:53.496
The new satellites will carry fully digital navigation payloads, inter-satellite links,

00:08:53.716 --> 00:08:57.556
and improved atomic clocks, with delivery scheduled for 2031.

00:08:58.256 --> 00:09:03.376
The satellites will join 38 first-generation spacecraft already in orbit or under construction.

00:09:04.036 --> 00:09:08.976
Galileo remains the world's most precise satellite navigation system, serving billions

00:09:08.976 --> 00:09:14.692
of users since its open service began in 2016. Astroscale has proposed that

00:09:14.692 --> 00:09:18.832
technologies developed for debris removal and satellite servicing could be

00:09:18.832 --> 00:09:24.252
repurposed into fleets of protective spacecraft. Space.com reports, the concept

00:09:24.252 --> 00:09:28.192
aims to shield high-value satellites from deliberate orbital attacks using

00:09:28.192 --> 00:09:32.872
existing rendezvous and capture hardware. The approach would leverage proven

00:09:32.872 --> 00:09:37.292
proximity operations and capture mechanisms already tested on debris removal

00:09:37.292 --> 00:09:41.432
missions. No new fundamental technologies would be required for the initial

00:09:41.432 --> 00:09:45.815
demonstrations. Beetlejuice's recently discovered companion star,

00:09:46.115 --> 00:09:51.035
C. Warha, is stirring the red Super Giants outer atmosphere in new radio observations.

00:09:51.695 --> 00:09:55.635
The disturbances appear as subtle velocity shifts and structural changes in

00:09:55.635 --> 00:09:59.095
the extended envelope. The companion's gravitational influence

00:09:59.095 --> 00:10:02.995
creates measurable perturbations that propagate through the star's outer layers.

00:10:03.655 --> 00:10:07.455
Continued monitoring will track how these disturbances evolve over multiple

00:10:07.455 --> 00:10:12.044
stellar rotation periods. New modeling published in Nature Geoscience

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:17.564
suggests rocky pebbles reacting with a hydrogen-rich early atmosphere could have produced much of

00:10:17.564 --> 00:10:22.804
Earth's water in situ. The same process may operate on other rocky planets forming around

00:10:22.804 --> 00:10:28.144
young stars. Hydrogen from the proto-planetary disk would have interacted with silicate minerals

00:10:28.144 --> 00:10:32.744
in the growing planetesimals. The resulting water could have been incorporated directly

00:10:32.744 --> 00:10:35.544
into the mantle and later released through volcanism.

00:10:36.283 --> 00:10:41.123
In brief, NASA Administrator Jared Isaacman will participate in a Caltech discussion

00:10:41.123 --> 00:10:43.023
on the future of space exploration.

00:10:43.723 --> 00:10:49.283
Astronauts Aneel and Kutrick will conduct a spacewalk on October 29th to install a new solar

00:10:49.283 --> 00:10:51.263
array on the International Space Station.

00:10:51.863 --> 00:10:57.223
A daily cloud forms and dissipates above RC amons during Mars' dusty season, stretching

00:10:57.223 --> 00:10:59.303
roughly 1,800 kilometers.

00:10:59.303 --> 00:11:04.523
The October 29th spacewalk will show whether a Neil and Kutrick get that new international

00:11:04.523 --> 00:11:06.703
space station solar array installed.

